*.pyc
trades.csv
oos_raw_output.txt

# Frozen bars for reproducible backtests (bar_cache.py). Local by design:
# committing them would make the repo the data store and the diffs unreadable.
.bar_cache/

# forward_log.jsonl is DELIBERATELY TRACKED, not ignored.
#
# A hash chain cannot detect its own tail being cut — drop the last row and
# what remains verifies clean, so the most recent trades are exactly what the
# chain does not protect. Git is the external anchor: committing the log after
# each scan makes a truncation visible as a deletion in the diff. Adding it
# here would remove the only protection it has.
